    <item>
      <title>bookshelf</title>
      <link>https://www.nickybu.blog/garden/bookshelf/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 06 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://www.nickybu.blog/garden/bookshelf/</guid>
      <description>a collection of my favourite books and what I&amp;rsquo;m currently reading</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Follow me on <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/75434680-nicky">goodreads</a></p>
<h2 id="books-im-currently-reading">books I&rsquo;m currently reading&hellip;</h2>


  <ul class="currently-reading-list">
    
      <li>The Greatest Show on Earth: The Evidence for Evolution by Richard Dawkins</li>
    
      <li>Planetes Omnibus, Volume 1 (Planetes, #1-2) by Makoto Yukimura</li>
    
      <li>Principles of Neural Science by Eric R. Kandel</li>
    
  </ul>


<h2 id="favourite-books">favourite books</h2>
<p>A collection of some of my favourite books &amp; graphic novels. Inspired by <a href="http://nickcammarata.com/bookshelf">Nick Cammarata’s</a> and <a href="https://visakanv.com/bookshelf/">Visa Kanv’s</a> bookshelves.</p>
<hr>
<p>What Mad Pursuit: A Personal View of Scientific Discovery - Francis Crick</p>
<p>From Bacteria to Bach and Back - Daniel Dennett</p>
<p>The Structure of Scientific Revolutions - Thomas S. Kuhn</p>
<p>The Grand Illusion: A Psychonautical Odyssey Into the Depths of Human Experience - Steven Lehar</p>
<p>Being You - Anil Seth</p>
<p>Surely You’re Only Joking Mr Feynman - Richard Feynman</p>
<p>The Metamorphosis of Prime Intellect - Roger Williams</p>
<p>The Sandman - Neil Gaiman</p>
<p>Solaris - Stanislaw Lem</p>
<p>American Psycho - Bret Easton Ellis</p>
<p>The Hitchhiker’s Guide To The Galaxy - Douglas Adams</p>
<p>Contact - Carl Sagan</p>
<p>Oranges - John McPhee</p>
<p>Ender’s Game - Orson Scott Card</p>
<p>The Stranger - Albert Camus</p>
<p>Hallucinations - Oliver Sacks</p>
<p>The Black Cloud - Fred Hoyle</p>
<p>Factotum - Charles Bukowski</p>
]]></content:encoded>
